<urn:atm:triage:finding/RBQA-F101-AW3>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RBQA-F101-AW3" ;
  triage:title "/v1/diagnostics and /v1/health return runtime-private response types instead of the manifest-declared ApiResponse/AtmError contract" ;
  triage:description "qa-pr1182-r2 ruthless-boundary-qa (quality-mgr msg 01M1QZ1W1KA2JM9M0YKMQ4XG1E, independently confirmed by quality-mgr). boundaries/atm-http-runtime/http-runtime.toml [contracts] (lines 37-41) states no runtime-private request, response, error, or persistence type is authorized, but diagnostics_route.rs ships DiagnosticsResponse/DiagnosticRecord/DiagnosticsError and health_route.rs ships HealthResponse as bespoke types; the TOML was not updated to match. Fix: either route the AW.3 read-only responses through the authorized atm-core ApiResponse/AtmError contract, or (if the sprint doc intends a dedicated read-only contract) declare it explicitly in the manifest with a quality-mgr-reviewed rationale. Fold into the AW3-QA-I1 remediation." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-aw" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "boundary" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
